OL,3,GNEWSABrother's shock as sister dies of
OL,4,Acancer in 24 days
OL,5,
OL,6,FA man whose sister died just 24 days
OL,7,Fafter being diagnosed with blood
OL,8,Fcancer, has spoken of how he went from
OL,9,Fplanning her recovery to arranging her
OL,10,Ffuneral in less than a month.
OL,12,FJeff Farnes, from Redditch,
OL,13,FWorcestershire, said doctors initially
OL,14,Fbelieved his sister Helen Bryan's acute
OL,15,Fmyeloid leukaemia (AML) had been caught
OL,16,Fearly and could be treated.
OL,18,FBut despite an encouraging prognosis
OL,19,Fand weeks of treatment that appeared to
OL,20,Fbe going well, the 57-year-old died
OL,21,Fless than a month after receiving the
OL,22,Fdiagnosis.
OL,23,APub: 03-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBC Eng (W) NewsCReg TVFWeather
